00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:37.600
Level 87? Can it be?

00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:41.800
I thought it was only a legend,
but the sprunjer never lies.

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:49.900
- It's in his pants!
- What the hell are you talking about?

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:01.000
Faster, faster!

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:03.700
I'm science-ing as fast as I can.

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:14.400
What do you say, folks? Hot or not?

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:17.800
I'm not seeing any information.
Do more things!

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:27.100
You, boogerbot,
read the code or I'll shoot this guy.

00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:30.800
- Who the hell is he?
- I'm Scruffy, the janitor.

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:32.400
Hang on, Scruffy!

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:35.800
''Zero, zero, one, one, zero, zero, zero,
one, zero, zero, one, zero,

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:38.800
''zero, one, one, one, one, zero,
one, zero, zero, zero, zero,

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:42.200
''one, one, zero, one, one, zero,
one, one, one, zero, zero, one, one.''

00:19:59.000 --> 00:20:00.500
A time sphere.

00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:02.800
Naked brothers, we have sprunjed

00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:06.000
upon the universal machine
language time code.

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:08.400
The key to time travel.

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:13.100
What's the secret of time travel doing
on Fry's ass?

00:20:13.200 --> 00:20:14.800
It was bound to be somewhere.

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:19.200
Beyond this shimmering portal lie
all the glories of history.

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:20.500
And we can steal them!

00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:24.500
We just go to the past and take stuff
with our superior weapons!

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:31.300
Stop, you fools.

00:20:32.400 --> 00:20:34.300
- What's going on?
- What is happening?

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:36.800
Nibbler, you... You can talk?

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:40.000
I can do more than talk. I can pontificate.

00:20:40.100 --> 00:20:42.300
You must not use the code of codes.

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:46.100
With each and every use,
you risk tearing the universe asunder.

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:48.900
Oh, he's so adorable.

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:50.800
The poodle-monkey may be right.

00:20:50.900 --> 00:20:54.400
The legend warns that the code is
powerful and dangerous.

00:20:54.500 --> 00:20:56.100
My God.

00:20:56.200 --> 00:20:58.700
We'd better use it only three or four times.
Six, max.

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:01.300
But even a single use could shatter
the universe.

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:03.500
Got it. Two or three times.

00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:05.900
I see I have no choice.

00:21:06.600 --> 00:21:08.800
Nibblonians, attack!

00:21:16.100 --> 00:21:17.900
Hey! That tickles.

00:21:22.600 --> 00:21:24.200
And the pitch!

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:27.500
Mayday, mayday!

00:21:37.100 --> 00:21:38.700
Hey! Hey! Hey!

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:43.000
Scamper!

00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:54.700
Alas, our kitten-class attack ships
were no match for their mighty chairs.

00:21:54.800 --> 00:21:57.600
The universe is doomed. Doomed!

00:21:57.700 --> 00:21:59.400
Can I pull up my pants now?

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:01.600
Doomed!

00:22:06.700 --> 00:22:08.600
Stand back, you wing wangs.

00:22:08.700 --> 00:22:12.700
I'm gonna try out this time sphere
with a quick test drive to yesterday.

00:22:12.800 --> 00:22:17.900
Bushwa! You can't go mucking about
in the past without creating paradoxes.

00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:22.000
I'm afraid he can.
It's a paradox-correcting time code.

00:22:22.100 --> 00:22:26.300
It all works perfectly.
Except when it rips open the universe!

00:22:26.400 --> 00:22:28.100
Don't do it. I beg you.

00:22:31.200 --> 00:22:33.800
Yesterday, please. And make it snappy!

00:22:36.700 --> 00:22:38.200
- Hello!
- Howdy!

00:22:38.300 --> 00:22:39.500
- Say, what the...
- That's weird.

00:22:39.600 --> 00:22:42.500
There was one, but now there's two.

00:22:42.600 --> 00:22:44.600
Nothing gets past you, eagle eye.

00:22:44.700 --> 00:22:48.400
I went back to last night
and met the ''me'' of that time for a drink.

00:22:48.500 --> 00:22:51.500
One thing led to another,
and we ended up at my place.

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:54.400
Or should I say our place?

00:22:57.200 --> 00:22:59.200
Oh, come on, you bunch of prudes!

00:22:59.300 --> 00:23:03.100
This isn't merely revolting,
it's impossible to boot.

00:23:03.200 --> 00:23:06.000
I know a paradox when I see one.

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:15.700
Paradox resolved. Someone get a mop!

00:23:26.100 --> 00:23:27.400
You're looking well, Pops.

00:23:27.500 --> 00:23:29.600
How can you look me in the eye-and-eye
and say that?

00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:33.500
I'm nothing but a brain.
A useless filthy brain!

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:35.800
You forgot lice-infested.

00:23:35.900 --> 00:23:38.200
I didn't forget, I just chose not to...

00:23:38.400 --> 00:23:39.900
Barbados Slim?

00:23:41.500 --> 00:23:42.700
What are you doing here?

00:23:42.800 --> 00:23:45.100
Is there something going on
between you two?

00:23:45.200 --> 00:23:46.700
Oh, no. No, no, no.

00:23:46.800 --> 00:23:51.300
We just happened to run into each other
shortly after your accident.

00:23:51.400 --> 00:23:53.600
And every night since then.

00:23:55.200 --> 00:23:56.200
You're so crazy.

00:23:56.400 --> 00:23:58.200
Woman, no!

00:23:58.300 --> 00:24:02.200
Oh, who am I kidding?
Without my body, I'm a nobody.

00:24:02.300 --> 00:24:08.500
I'm sorry, Hermes. But look at Barbados.
You can't argue with those luscious pecs.

00:24:08.600 --> 00:24:10.000
No, I can't.

00:24:10.100 --> 00:24:13.100
But I can ask him to stop wiggling them
in my face.

00:24:13.200 --> 00:24:16.900
I'm not wiggling them.
They do that by themselves.

00:24:20.400 --> 00:24:24.000
I think I'll go back in time and steal
the Liberty Bell before it cracked.

00:24:24.100 --> 00:24:27.800
- Or is the crack the valuable part?
- I don't know, you naked crook!

00:24:27.900 --> 00:24:31.000
We have a problem, Nudar.
It's a one-way time code.

00:24:31.100 --> 00:24:34.800
It can take us to the past,
but it can't bring us back to the present!

00:24:36.600 --> 00:24:39.700
Masters, if I might?
Let me do the stealing.

00:24:39.800 --> 00:24:43.900
I'll go to the past and snatch everything
I can get my greasy mitts on.

00:24:44.000 --> 00:24:47.600
Then, as a robot,
I can just wait it out for a few centuries

00:24:47.700 --> 00:24:50.100
in the limestone cavern
beneath this building.

00:24:50.200 --> 00:24:52.600
Oh, it'll be ever so much fun!

00:24:52.700 --> 00:24:54.100
Hey, that's perfect.

00:24:54.200 --> 00:24:57.000
We sit back and let
dumb-dumb here do the stealing.

00:24:57.100 --> 00:24:59.200
Dumb-dumb away!

00:24:59.800 --> 00:25:01.400
Zero, zero, one, one, zero, zero...

00:25:04.500 --> 00:25:05.800
Yup!

00:25:09.200 --> 00:25:10.800
The Mona Lisa!

00:25:10.900 --> 00:25:12.600
Sorry, it's not quite finished.

00:25:12.700 --> 00:25:14.100
Da Vinci give you any trouble?

00:25:14.200 --> 00:25:17.600
Let's just say he may not
make it to The Last Supper.

00:25:18.900 --> 00:25:22.500
Preposterous twaddlecock!
Time travel is impossible.

00:25:22.600 --> 00:25:24.300
But, Professor, you time-traveled yourself.

00:25:24.400 --> 00:25:26.400
Remember,
when we went back to Roswell?

00:25:26.500 --> 00:25:27.900
That proves nothing.

00:25:28.000 --> 00:25:31.200
And, furthermore, you'd think
I'd remember a thing like that.

00:25:31.300 --> 00:25:33.300
Plus, who are you, anyway?

00:25:33.400 --> 00:25:37.900
- Man, this is fun on a bun! Here I go again!
- Oh, no, you don't!

00:25:38.100 --> 00:25:39.000
Zero, zero, one, one...

00:25:47.200 --> 00:25:49.700
Scarab, forearm, bird, bird, bird.

00:25:54.400 --> 00:25:56.400
No, it's just me, Bender.

00:25:58.900 --> 00:26:00.900
I must tell you, Hedonismbot,

00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:05.100
I hate to sell my doomsday devices
to a private collector.

00:26:05.200 --> 00:26:09.200
But with my business stolen,
I have to make ends meet.

00:26:09.400 --> 00:26:10.800
You will be careful?

00:26:10.900 --> 00:26:15.700
I shan't touch them till I've had Jambi
lock the absinthe and ether away.

00:26:15.800 --> 00:26:20.700
- Oh! What does this one do?
- That one kills everything everywhere.

00:26:21.400 --> 00:26:24.300
How delightful. And this one?

00:26:24.400 --> 00:26:27.200
Sir, the spheroboom is not for sale.

00:26:29.400 --> 00:26:31.800
It's my sentimental favorite.

00:26:32.400 --> 00:26:37.200
No need to explain.
I, too, have known unconventional love.

00:26:37.300 --> 00:26:40.300
Perhaps you and I and Jambi
could get together

00:26:40.500 --> 00:26:42.200
and compare notes sometime, eh?

00:26:46.600 --> 00:26:51.000
Resulting in peace between
East and West Coast rappers...

00:26:51.500 --> 00:26:52.800
Good God!

00:26:53.200 --> 00:26:56.800
I accept this Nobel Peace Prize
not just for myself,

00:26:56.900 --> 00:26:59.900
but for crime robots everywhere. Skoal!

00:27:10.900 --> 00:27:13.000
Not so neutral now, are you, Sweden?

00:27:27.200 --> 00:27:29.800
Be honest with me.
Does my eye look monstery?

00:27:29.900 --> 00:27:32.100
I don't want to look monstery
for my date with Lars.

00:27:32.200 --> 00:27:34.200
At least a monster has a body.

00:27:34.300 --> 00:27:38.500
What I wouldn't give for Wolf Man's torso,
or any of the Groovie Goolies.

00:27:39.200 --> 00:27:43.100
I think I'll wear that slutty dress
I've been saving for Easter.

00:27:44.100 --> 00:27:48.000
I'd like to punch Lars right
in his ruggedly good-looking face.

00:27:53.400 --> 00:27:56.800
Like all rich people, we're gonna need
weapons to shoot poor people.

00:27:56.900 --> 00:27:59.200
- In self-defense?
- Yes, that, too.

00:27:59.300 --> 00:28:02.200
Bender, go steal the doomsday device
chained to the professor's wrist.

00:28:02.300 --> 00:28:03.400
Never!

00:28:03.800 --> 00:28:07.500
I'm kidding. You guys know
I have to do whatever you say.

00:28:07.600 --> 00:28:11.700
- Here, swap this for the real one.
- The old switcheroo.

00:28:11.800 --> 00:28:13.700
Yes, but don't wake him.

00:28:13.800 --> 00:28:16.200
You'll need jeweler's tools
and foot-cup silencers.

00:28:16.300 --> 00:28:18.900
Hey. I don't tell you how
to tell me what to do,

00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:21.900
so don't tell me how to do
what you tell me to do.

00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:24.900
Bender knows when to use finesse.

00:28:26.300 --> 00:28:29.200
- Here you go.
- Put it in the safe, clanky.

00:28:35.000 --> 00:28:36.700
It's the damnedest thing.

00:28:36.800 --> 00:28:40.400
There I was in the dumpster,
enjoying a moldy Fudgsicle,

00:28:40.500 --> 00:28:43.800
when suddenly your hand flies
over and slaps me in the toches.

00:28:43.900 --> 00:28:46.600
Yes, well, these things happen.

00:28:46.700 --> 00:28:50.300
Fortunately, the spheroboom is still safe.

00:28:53.100 --> 00:28:57.000
Scammed? Me? Sweetheart?

00:29:00.800 --> 00:29:03.000
You do a nice hand job, Zoidberg.

00:29:03.100 --> 00:29:07.300
Tell me, if I could find an undamaged body,
could you recapitate me?

00:29:07.400 --> 00:29:09.100
Hermes, I'm a surgeon.

00:29:09.200 --> 00:29:10.500
When I see two body parts,

00:29:10.600 --> 00:29:13.300
I sew them together
and see what happens.

00:29:15.000 --> 00:29:16.900
All I'm asking is for you to go back in time

00:29:17.000 --> 00:29:19.600
to when I still had my body
and bring it back for me.

00:29:19.700 --> 00:29:23.000
- What do I do with your old head?
- I don't care in the slightest.

00:29:23.100 --> 00:29:24.300
Can do!

00:29:27.600 --> 00:29:30.300
- Come on, man!
- Hermes, please!

00:29:30.400 --> 00:29:32.800
You can't hurry
a delicate operation like this.

00:29:39.500 --> 00:29:41.000
What are those?

00:29:41.600 --> 00:29:43.700
You incompetent crab!

00:29:43.800 --> 00:29:47.000
I thought you were happy.
Your tail was wagging.

00:29:55.500 --> 00:29:59.800
I believe this paradoxicality
equation to be unsolvable.

00:29:59.900 --> 00:30:02.400
Ergo, time travel is impossible.

00:30:02.500 --> 00:30:04.600
But I can't quite prove it, Bubblegum.

00:30:04.700 --> 00:30:08.400
Perhaps you and your razzle-dazzle
Globetrotter calculus could...

00:30:08.500 --> 00:30:10.900
Looks pretty damn solvable to me, Farnsy.

00:30:11.000 --> 00:30:15.200
Sweet Clyde, use variation of parameters
and expand the Wronskian.

00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:28.100
Shizz, baby.

00:30:28.200 --> 00:30:31.900
So paradox-free time travel
is possible after all.

00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:34.800
Right on. But dig this multiplicand here.

00:30:34.900 --> 00:30:39.200
The ''doom field''? That must be
what corrects the paradoxes.

00:30:39.300 --> 00:30:41.400
But that mama rises exponentially.

00:30:41.500 --> 00:30:44.500
It could rupture
the very fabric of causality.

00:30:44.600 --> 00:30:47.200
That's what I've been trying to tell you.

00:30:51.700 --> 00:30:53.900
Hermes! You got your body back.

00:30:55.400 --> 00:30:57.500
Yes, but not the original.

00:30:57.600 --> 00:30:59.900
Bender went back in time
and picked up a copy.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:02.600
A copy? Funky cold medina!

00:31:02.700 --> 00:31:05.500
According to this equation,
a time-travel duplicate

00:31:05.600 --> 00:31:09.200
results in a complex denominator
in the causality ratio.

00:31:09.300 --> 00:31:13.100
- Oh, snap! You know what that means.
- I can guess.

00:31:13.800 --> 00:31:15.600
Actually, I can't guess.

00:31:15.700 --> 00:31:18.500
Prof, you got a doom meter in this lab?

00:31:21.700 --> 00:31:23.300
Good Lord, Bubblegum.

00:31:23.400 --> 00:31:28.100
The duplicate body is emitting doom
at 10 times the background level.

00:31:28.200 --> 00:31:32.000
I thought as much.
A duplicate body is always doomed.

00:31:32.100 --> 00:31:33.600
It's just a matter of time.

00:31:33.700 --> 00:31:37.700
I don't care. I just need it long enough
to bird-dog in and win LaBarbara back.

00:31:37.800 --> 00:31:42.300
- Best bird-dog fast, my brother.
- That's the way I bird-dog best.

00:31:47.600 --> 00:31:50.100
Drink, quick!
I can't balance it much longer.

00:31:50.200 --> 00:31:51.600
Wait, I...

00:31:52.100 --> 00:31:53.300
Yes!

00:31:53.400 --> 00:31:55.500
Oh, this is so much fun, Lars.

00:31:55.600 --> 00:31:57.300
Most men are intimidated by the fact

00:31:57.400 --> 00:31:59.500
that I could kill them
with a flick of my wrist.

00:31:59.600 --> 00:32:02.500
Well, not me, 'cause if you do,
you'll be stuck with the check.

00:32:04.000 --> 00:32:06.500
Folks, you care for
a little fresh ground Executive?

00:32:06.600 --> 00:32:08.200
Please.

00:32:16.800 --> 00:32:20.600
Don't get excited, kids.
This thing's got heart-shaped nostrils.

00:32:20.700 --> 00:32:21.900
Want to see it make a star?

00:32:22.000 --> 00:32:23.000
- No!
- No!

00:33:33.600 --> 00:33:37.600
Here's your Gutenberg Bible, masters.
Plus, the Colonel's secret recipe.

00:33:39.200 --> 00:33:43.200
Well, that does it.
We've got every valuable object in history.

00:33:46.500 --> 00:33:49.600
Now that I'm rich, I suddenly care
if the universe gets destroyed.

00:33:49.700 --> 00:33:52.100
We can't use
that dangerous time code again.

00:33:52.200 --> 00:33:54.100
Blank it from the robot's memory.

00:33:55.200 --> 00:33:58.200
I'll vaporize this guy so his ass
doesn't fall into the wrong hands.

00:33:59.400 --> 00:34:01.100
Why don't you just remove my tattoo?

00:34:01.200 --> 00:34:03.500
Nice try,
but you might have memorized it.

00:34:03.600 --> 00:34:04.500
No, I mightn't.

00:34:04.700 --> 00:34:07.100
I can't even remember
my mother's maiden name.

00:34:07.200 --> 00:34:08.700
It's Gleissner.

00:34:11.000 --> 00:34:13.900
Stupid naked aliens. Stupid Lars.

00:34:14.000 --> 00:34:15.700
I hate the future.

00:34:21.800 --> 00:34:25.000
Man, that cube root was
a real buzzer-beater, Clyde.

00:34:25.700 --> 00:34:30.500
Zero, one, one, one, zero, zero, one, one!

00:34:32.700 --> 00:34:33.700
Blast him!

00:34:38.600 --> 00:34:41.200
You missed. Oh, great master.

00:34:49.900 --> 00:34:51.300
Hello, 2000.

00:34:51.800 --> 00:34:53.100
I'm home.

00:34:53.200 --> 00:34:55.500
Happy New Year, naked weirdo!

00:34:56.200 --> 00:34:57.900
Happy New Year.

00:35:03.100 --> 00:35:05.400
Well, we'll never know
where the ass guy went,

00:35:05.500 --> 00:35:08.500
and since we can't kill him,
I say live and let live.

00:35:08.900 --> 00:35:10.500
That's sweet, boss.

00:35:10.600 --> 00:35:13.300
Fry'll be nice and cozy
back in the year 2000.

00:35:13.400 --> 00:35:15.900
What? How do you know
he went to the year 2000?

00:35:16.000 --> 00:35:17.900
That's where he always goes.

00:35:18.600 --> 00:35:22.200
Better play it safe.
Go there a little earlier and wait for him.

00:35:22.300 --> 00:35:24.300
You know what to do.

00:35:24.400 --> 00:35:28.700
You want me to concludify him
like some sort of dispatcherator?

00:35:28.800 --> 00:35:31.500
- Yes, and don't forget to terminate him.
- Got it.

00:35:31.600 --> 00:35:35.300
Preparing to terminate Philip Fry.

00:35:35.400 --> 00:35:37.400
What's with the doofy sunglasses?

00:35:37.500 --> 00:35:39.600
It's really bright in the past.

00:35:39.700 --> 00:35:42.000
Zero, zero, one, one, zero...

00:35:50.300 --> 00:35:53.200
Okay, Fry. Come to papa.

00:35:55.500 --> 00:35:57.000
Man, I'm bored.

00:36:06.200 --> 00:36:07.900
Hey, there you are.

00:36:09.900 --> 00:36:13.400
Oh, wait.
That's Fry before he goes to the future.

00:36:13.500 --> 00:36:16.900
I'm waiting for the one
who comes back from the future.

00:36:17.600 --> 00:36:19.000
Jeez, this is confusing.

00:36:19.400 --> 00:36:22.600
And I bet it's gonna get
a lot more confusing.

00:36:25.200 --> 00:36:27.500
That cheap beer
really goes right through you.

00:36:27.600 --> 00:36:30.200
For the first time ever,
I gotta use the bathroom.

00:36:30.300 --> 00:36:31.900
But if I leave, I might miss Fry.

00:36:33.100 --> 00:36:34.400
Unless...

00:36:35.200 --> 00:36:37.200
Zero, zero,
one, one, zero, zero...

00:36:40.900 --> 00:36:43.700
And I bet it's gonna get
a lot more confusing.

00:36:45.000 --> 00:36:48.100
Hi, I'm you from 19 seconds in the future.

00:36:48.200 --> 00:36:51.000
Stay here and wait for Fry
while I go to the bathroom.

00:36:51.100 --> 00:36:52.500
Okay, boss.

00:36:52.600 --> 00:36:54.700
After I kill Fry, you're next.

00:36:54.800 --> 00:36:56.400
- What?
- Nothing.

00:36:59.400 --> 00:37:01.100
What the... Who are you?

00:37:01.200 --> 00:37:03.000
I'm Bender from way at the end.

00:37:03.100 --> 00:37:06.400
I came back to put
this rub-on time code on Fry's ass.

00:37:06.500 --> 00:37:08.400
So what are you now, a butler?

00:37:08.800 --> 00:37:11.000
Spot of tea, please, jerk wad.

